## Summary

xAI's announcement describes bots with their own computers, access to tools
and apps, persistent ongoing work, conversational memory, and
approval-based escalation to the human.

## Why it matters to ATL

This is the product-level version of what ATL builds by hand: persistent
teammates that remember context across sessions and escalate for approval.
ATL already has the approval gate (owner gates, `atl approve`) and durable
state; the deltas are persistent agent identity/memory across sessions and
the teammate-facing surface.

## ATL recommendation

P1: keep ATL's explicit-file memory (state.json + learning.json) but study
Grok Bot's escalation UX and teammate pages for the control room. File
follow-up records when the TUI wave lands.
